{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>My words, give ear</b> — from the root of אזנים (ears); incline Your ear." "<b>Consider</b> — imperative form, like שימה נא (please set)." "<b>My sighing</b> — doubled in the ayin, for it is from הגא, like זנוניה, and he said to HaShem בינה (consider), in the manner of human speech, and similarly ודע לבבי (and know my heart), also האזינה (give ear). And the reason is that it be made clear to all, for there is no doubt that He knows all, and He has no need of ears, as He who planted the ear — shall He not hear?" "<b>Give heed</b> — this root-form is bound with a lamed, therefore it is incorrect to say מי יקשיבני (who will give heed to me)." "And the meaning of <b>my King</b> — I have no king to whom I might cry for help, only You alone."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:25.855413874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}